<%# locals: (form:, filter:, path:, disabled: false, hint: nil) %>
<%# A range of dates to filter a list by, for a page's GET form: From and To as date fields, the presets as links and an Apply button. `filter` is a DateRangeFilter, and its dates are what the fields start as (the current month, when it couldn't use what was sent). The fields are named `filter[date_from]` and `filter[date_to]`, so the form's scope is `filter`, and the page's other filters are fields of the same form, or hidden ones. %>
<%# A preset is a link to the same page with the other filters kept and these two dates set: `path` turns a preset's params into the address. The one the range equals is marked with aria-current and filled dark, and not only coloured. Nothing is submitted until Apply is, so there's no JavaScript. %>
<%# An `optional` range (a list that doesn't need one, such as Unfiled bank transactions) starts with both fields empty and not required, any date, which is its first preset; with a date in one and not the other it's an alert and any date, never an empty page. %>
<%# `disabled` is for a page whose state doesn't use the range, such as the unfiled bank transactions, which are listed whatever their date: the fields are shown disabled, so they send nothing, the presets have nothing to set and are left out, and `hint` says why, in words the fields are described by. %>
<% hint_id = form.field_id(:date_range, :hint) if hint %>
<div class="space-y-4">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
    <% { date_from: [ "From", filter.from ], date_to: [ "To", filter.to ] }.each do |attribute, (label, date)| %>
      <%= render "components/field", form: form, attribute: attribute, label: label do |field| %>
        <%= form.date_field attribute, value: DateRangeFilter.spell(date), required: !disabled && !filter.optional?, disabled: disabled,
              **field.merge(aria: field[:aria].merge(describedby: [ field.dig(:aria, :describedby), hint_id ].compact.join(" ").presence)) %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <% if hint %>
    <p id="<%= hint_id %>" class="text-sm text-base-content/70"><%= hint %></p>
  <% end %>

  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
    <% unless disabled %>
      <% filter.presets.each do |preset| %>
        <% current = filter.preset == preset.key %>
        <%= link_to preset.label, path.call(preset.params), class: class_names("btn btn-sm", "btn-neutral": current), aria: { current: ("true" if current) } %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
    <%= form.submit "Apply", name: nil, class: "btn btn-sm btn-primary" %>
  </div>
</div>
